TXT-capable providers with zone discovery now store ownership in compressed pages and per-owner manifests by default. Ownership remains in DNS, with no volume or database requirement. Distinct active owners retain each other's compatible claims; incomplete or conflicting state prevents destructive reconciliation. Upgrade shared-zone writers in `legacy` mode before enabling compact storage. Selecting `legacy` on the new binary verifies restored per-member markers before removing compact claims. Same-owner replicas and simultaneous writes to provider APIs that replace whole RRsets still require provider-specific coordination. See the ownership storage guide for migration headroom and recovery limits.
